med from inside the test stage, so CAT-02 now waits for your decision. I didn't change any code, any test, or the plan, and I didn't run the gate again.\n\n**What failed:** the `tests-kept` check refused `BaseE2ETest.java`. This story didn't change that file. The plan gate saved its copy of the existing tests at 00:35. Your commit `33236c6` at 08:01 then changed the file: it's how you carried out the CAT-01-01 answer that the browser suite starts the shop itself. The file now uses `ShopUnderTest.baseUrl()` instead of `localhost:8080`.\n\n**Why the test stage can't fix it:**\n- Putting the old lines back would undo that commit, and the whole browser suite, including CAT-02's own `ProductPageE2ETest`, depends on it.\n- Listing the file under `## Changed tests` means editing `plan.md`, which only the plan stage writes.\n- The story has no `## Changed expectations` section, and apart from that the gate only accepts an answered decision.\n\n**What I wrote:**\n- `.agents/factory/decisions/CAT-02-01.md`: the question, with three options:\n  - **a:** answer the decision to accept the change. This is my recommendation; nothing else needs to change.\n  - **b:** re-run the plan stage so the plan lists the file.\n  - **c:** delete the saved copy (`tasks/CAT-02/.tests-baseline`) and pass the plan gate again, so the copy includes the commit.\n- `tasks/CAT-02/tests.md`: a new `## needs-human` section that points to that decision.\n\nTo unblock it, answer CAT-02-01 with `/factory-decisions`, then run the test stage again.","ttft_ms":3839,"type":"result","duration_ms":60119,"uuid":"b42fe20b-31f6-46ce-a4a4-cfaea4317fab","ttft_stream_ms":3197,"time_to_request_ms":40,"first_content_frame_ms":3197,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
